{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '2818,2864p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '1178,1210p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js && ls -lh evidence/results.png evidence/mixed-and-flower-warning.png evidence/finale.png\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '2818,2864p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js && sed -n '1178,1210p' vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js && ls -lh evidence/results.png evidence/mixed-and-flower-warning.png evidence/finale.png\"","aggregated_output":"      if (live && o.min && now() - t0 < o.min * 1000) { requestAnimationFrame(next); return; }\n      if (live) BOOT._step(n + 1, n + 1, 'Warming up');\n      this._booting = false; const bg = this._bootGo; this._bootGo = null;\n      if (bg && h.scenes && h.scenes[bg.name]) Object.assign(h, { scene: bg.name, data: bg.data }); else if (bg) warn('go:' + bg.name, 'game.go(\"' + bg.name + '\") in a boot step: no such scene. Scenes: ' + Object.keys(h.scenes || {}).join(', '));\n      this.start(h); res(this);\n    };\n    next();\n    return this;\n  }\n  /** stop the loop; the game keeps its state, and start() resumes it */\n  stop() { this._running = false; if (this._raf != null && typeof cancelAnimationFrame === 'function') cancelAnimationFrame(this._raf); this._raf = null; return this; }\n  /**\n   * end the game for good: stop the loop and remove everything the engine added to the page (its listeners on the window,\n   * the document, the canvas and the buttons, the touch controls, the GPU lighting's canvas) and close the sound. Tests and\n   * tools that make many games call it; the canvas stays\n   */\n  dispose() {\n    /** disposed: true after dispose() */\n    this.stop(); this.disposed = true;\n    if (this._abort) this._abort.abort();\n    if (this.shell) this.shell.dispose();\n    const A = this.audio; try { A.stopMusic(); if (A.ctx && A.ctx.close) A.ctx.close(); } catch (e) { /* already closed */ } A.ctx = null; A.failed = 'the game was disposed';\n    const I = this.input; I.stopRumble(); for (const el of [I._touchEl, I._stickEl, I._knobEl, this._corner]) if (el && el.remove) el.remove();\n    this._corner = null;\n    const G = this.gpu; if (G) { try { if (G._cv) G._cv.remove(); if (G._dev && G._dev.destroy) G._dev.destroy(); } catch (e) { /* gone */ } G.enabled = G.ready = false; this.gpu = null; }\n    if (E.current === this) E.current = null;\n  }\n  /**\n   * run the game for `seconds` of real time in exact fixed steps, at once, without requestAnimationFrame: tests, tools and\n   * headless runs (advance(1) is 120 updates). o.draw: then draw one frame (not in a headless game). A headless game made\n   * with draw: true draws one frame each advance, on a stand-in renderer, so a draw error lands in game.errors (a test\n   * that catches what a player would see break). Returns the updates run\n   */\n  advance(seconds = this.o.step, o = {}) {\n    if (!this.scene && !this._next) throw new Error('game.advance() needs a started game: game.start({ update, draw }) first');\n    this._acc += Math.max(0, seconds);\n    const n = this._steps(); this.stats.steps = n;\n    if (this.r && (this.headless ? this.o.draw : o.draw)) try { this._frame(); } catch (e) { this.fail('draw', e); }\n    return n;\n  }\n  /**\n   * the clock: an exact fixed step. Real time (at most 50 ms a frame, so a stall can't run away) fills an accumulator;\n   * each whole o.step of it (1/120 s) runs one update of o.step * timeScale game seconds (split in two or more when\n   * timeScale > 1, so no step is longer than o.step), and the remainder waits for the next frame (game.alpha = its\n   * fraction of a step). 60 Hz runs two steps a frame, 120 Hz one, 144 Hz one on most frames: the same steps at any rate.\n   * Slow motion makes steps shorter, never fewer. Paused or at timeScale 0 the steps still run (dt 0), so input ticks.\n   * The first frame always updates (with dt 0 when its time is short of a step), so draw never comes before update.\n      this.padIndex = p ? p.index : null; this.padId = p ? p.id : '';\n      if (this.aimSource === 'pad') this.aimSource = 'move';\n    }\n    if (p) {\n      const dz = (x, y) => { const l = Math.hypot(x, y), d = clamp(this.deadzone, 0, .8); return l <= d ? [0, 0] : [x / l * Math.min(1, (l - d) / (1 - d)), y / l * Math.min(1, (l - d) / (1 - d))]; };\n      this.padAxes = Array.from(p.axes);\n      this.padMove = dz(p.axes[0] || 0, p.axes[1] || 0); if (this.invertMoveX) this.padMove[0] *= -1; if (this.invertMoveY) this.padMove[1] *= -1;   // (the Controller settings: a stick worn the wrong way)\n      const aim = dz(p.axes[2] || 0, p.axes[3] || 0);\n      this.padAim = Math.hypot(...aim) > 0 ? [aim[0], aim[1] * (this.invertAimY ? -1 : 1)] : null;\n      this.padValues = p.buttons.map(b => b.value || (b.pressed ? 1 : 0));\n      const ra = this.padAim || [0, 0], rd = [ra[1] < -.5, ra[1] > .5, ra[0] < -.5, ra[0] > .5];\n      ['PadRAxisUp', 'PadRAxisDown', 'PadRAxisLeft', 'PadRAxisRight'].forEach((c, i) => rd[i] ? this.press(c) : this.release(c));   // (the right stick past halfway: codes to bind)\n      if (this.padAim || Math.hypot(...this.padMove) > 0) { this.aimSource = 'pad'; this.lastDevice = 'gamepad'; }\n      p.buttons.forEach((b, i) => { const on = b.pressed; if (on && !this.padPrev[i]) this.press('Pad' + i); if (!on && this.padPrev[i]) this.release('Pad' + i); this.padPrev[i] = on; });\n      const dirs = [this.padMove[1] < -.5, this.padMove[1] > .5, this.padMove[0] < -.5, this.padMove[0] > .5];\n      ['PadAxisUp', 'PadAxisDown', 'PadAxisLeft', 'PadAxisRight'].forEach((c, i) => dirs[i] ? this.press(c) : this.release(c));\n    }\n    // a tap is held for the one step after it (its release comes the step after that)\n    for (const c of this._tapsDue) if (!this._holds.has(c)) this.release(c);\n    const due = this._tapsDue; due.clear(); this._tapsDue = this._taps; this._taps = due;\n    // presses since the last step become this step's pressed()/released()\n    const n = this._now; n.clear(); this._now = this._fresh; this._fresh = n; this._freshCodes.clear();\n    const u = this._nowUp; u.clear(); this._nowUp = this._freshUp; this._freshUp = u;\n    this._clickAt = this._click; this._click = null; this._zoomNow = this._zoomAcc; this._zoomAcc = 1;\n    const G = this._g; if (G && !G.moved && !G.long && this.clock - G.t >= .45) { G.long = true; this._gLong = [G.x, G.y]; }   // a press held still\n    this._longAt = this._gLong; this._tap2At = this._gTap2; this._panAt = this._gPan; this._gLong = this._gTap2 = this._gPan = null;\n    this._boxAt = this._gBox && Object.assign({}, this._gBox); if (this._gBox && this._gBox.done) this._gBox = null;\n    const da = this._dragAcc || (this._dragAcc = [0, 0]), k = this.screen.dpr / this.screen.S; this._drag = this.stickOn ? [da[0] * k, da[1] * k] : null; da[0] = da[1] = 0;\n  }\n  /** wire every element with data-act=\"<action>\" inside root to the action */\n  bindButtons(root) {\n    this._boundButtons = (this._boundButtons || []).filter(b => b.isConnected);\n    root.querySelectorAll('[data-act]').forEach(b => {\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 54K Nov  6 05:23 evidence/finale.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 54K Nov  6 05:23 evidence/mixed-and-flower-warning.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 54K Nov  6 05:23 evidence/results.png\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='src/input.js';s=open(p).read();old=\\\"\\\"\\\"if(axes.some((v,i)=>Math.abs(v)>.065&&Math.abs(v-(old[i]||0))>.045)||q.anyPressed()){any=true;pointer=false;clearId=0;}\n        q._bcpAxes=axes.slice();\\\"\\\"\\\";new=\\\"\\\"\\\"const padChanged=axes.some((v,i)=>Math.abs(v)>.065&&Math.abs(v-(old[i]||0))>.045)||q.padPrev.some((on,i)=>on&&\"'!q._bcpButtons?.[i]);\n        if(padChanged){any=true;pointer=false;clearId=0;}else if(q.anyPressed())any=true;\n        q._bcpAxes=axes.slice();q._bcpButtons=q.padPrev.slice();\"\"\";assert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new);open(p,'\"'w').write(s)\np='src/main.js';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"res:[640,360],expand:true,\\\",\\\"res:[640,360],draw:true,expand:true,\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"    for(const q of game.players)q.clear();\\\",\\\"    for(const q of game.players){q.clear();q.padIndex=null;q.padId='';q.padPrev=[];if(q.pad===null)q.lastDevice='keyboard';}\\\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/screens.js';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"g.shell.root.classList.toggle('large-text',g.settings.tvScale>1);\\\",\\\"g.shell.root.classList.toggle('large-text',g.settings.tvScale>1);if(typeof window\"'!=='\"'undefined')window.dispatchEvent(new Event('resize'));\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/browser.py';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"def shot(page,name):page.screenshot(path=str(base/'evidence'/name))\\\",\\\"def shot(page,name):\\\\n page.evaluate('__game.advance(0,{draw:true})')\\\\n page.screenshot(path=str(base/'evidence'/name))\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"page.evaluate('__setPad(0,[2])');\\\",\\\"page.evaluate(\\\\\\\"BCP.placeComb(__BUZZ.world,430,3,false,'pad-call-proof');__setPad(0,[2])\\\\\\\");\\\",1)\ns=s.replace(\\\"page.keyboard.press('Enter');page.evaluate('__game.advance(.2)')\\\",\\\"page.evaluate('__game.advance(.3)');page.keyboard.press('Enter');page.evaluate('__game.advance(.2)')\\\")\n# Exact native screen-to-CSS round trip, not projected world coordinates.\nold=\\\"point=phone.evaluate(\\\\\\\"(()=>{const rc=__game.screen.canvas.getBoundingClientRect(),S=__game.screen;const a=S.clientToScreen(rc.left,rc.top),b=S.clientToScreen(rc.right,rc.bottom);const x=(__game.W-640)/2+320,y=(__game.H-360)/2+173;return {x:rc.left+(x-a[0])/(b[0]-a[0])*rc.width,y:rc.top+(y-a[1])/(b[1]-a[1])*rc.height};})()\\\\\\\")\\\"\nnew=\\\"point=phone.evaluate(\\\\\\\"(()=>{const s=__game.screen,rc=s.canvas.getBoundingClientRect(),x=(__game.W-640)/2+320,y=(__game.H-360)/2+173;return {x:rc.left+(x*s.S+s.OX)/s.dpr,y:rc.top+(y*s.S+s.OY)/s.dpr};})()\\\\\\\")\\\"\nassert old in s;s=s.replace(old,new)\ns=s.replace(\\\"phone.evaluate(\\\\\\\"__game.input.lastDevice='touch'; __BUZZ.world.obstacles=[];\\\",\\\"phone.evaluate(\\\\\\\"__game.input.lastDevice='touch';__BUZZ.world.bird.state='idle';__BUZZ.world.bird.timer=20; __BUZZ.world.obstacles=[];\\\")\n# live checkpoint to make a slow failure diagnosable without extra console noise.\ns=s.replace(\\\"checks.append({'name':name,'pass':bool(ok),'detail':str(detail) if not ok else ''})\\\", \\\"checks.append({'name':name,'pass':bool(ok),'detail':str(detail) if not ok else ''})\\\\n (base/'evidence/browser-live.json').write_text(json.dumps(checks))\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nimport json\np='docs/issues.json';items=json.load(open(p));items += [{'id':'I005','critical':False,'foundBy':'Controller/mouse browser checks and focused diagnostic','issue':'Generic input activity treated Mouse0 as pad activity and disabled mouse column aiming on spray.','fix':'Only new gamepad buttons or meaningful analog changes take ownership from the pointer.','verified':False},{'id':'I006','critical':False,'foundBy':'Controller-to-local-co-op browser check and native input inspection','issue':'Explicitly reassigning a pad to player 2 could be mistaken for a disconnected player 1 pad.','fix':'Reset device discovery state when committing an explicit seat configuration.','verified':False}]\nfor a in items:\n if a['id'] in ['I003','I004']:a['verified']=True\njson.dump(items,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nPY\nnode tools/build.mjs --quiet\n/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python tests/browser.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"agent_message","text":"Both Hub gameplay defects are fixed. The two-copy test now confirms shared conversion and scoring, remote bird calls, enclosure resets, departures, and a single terminal result. Controller and mouse checks also found an ownership bug: clicking spray canceled pointer aiming. That fix is in, and the device checks are running again.\n"}}
