e from native input\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"mouse aim and spray use bounded can travel\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"parked pointer does not fight keyboard movement\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"controller disconnect pauses standalone and explains recovery\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"attract waits until ten seconds of real idle\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"ten-second idle starts real simulation demonstration\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"keyboard attract wake is consumed at title\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"pointer movement interrupts attract and is consumed\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"analog movement below gameplay dead zone wakes attract\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"controller button wake cannot also start a run\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"attract and assisted play do not write normal records\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"assembled game ordinary-input whole campaign reaches real win card\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"unassisted full campaign updates local records once\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"win card can start a clean fresh run\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"keyboard plus pad assigns exclusive devices\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"one pad cannot control both co-op cans\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"shared keyboard controls simultaneous independent cans\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"code audio produces finite non-silent non-clipped output\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"music bus ten-percent gain and mute are correct\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"audio teardown stops generated voice nodes\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"Chromium session has no page or native game errors\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"touch drag steers the can with invisible controls\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"safe touch assistance fires useful ordinary spray\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"touch parcel tap exposes contextual actions\", \"pass\": false, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"touch menu opens native pause\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"orientation change preserves canonical arena geometry\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"touch rotation draws without native or page errors\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}, {\"name\": \"WebKit boots, takes input and draws native game without errors\", \"pass\": true, \"detail\": \"\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > tools/write-interview.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport {readFileSync,writeFileSync} from 'node:fs';\nconst root=new URL('../',import.meta.url),read=p=>JSON.parse(readFileSync(new URL(p,root),'utf8'));\nconst rel=read('release.json'),issues=read('docs/issues.json');\nconst data={\n sourceInformation:{\n  date:'2026-11-06 04:57:48',source:'Buzz Bombers (1983, Intellivision)',plan:'PLAN.md',genre:'Arcade garden shooter; tactical score attack',perspective:'Fixed front-facing 2D garden theater, rendered with the native overhead coordinate view',\n  tech:'JavaScript, HTML, Canvas 2D; my-3D2dge 0.89.1 at 8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691 with documented actor-bounds and Fill patches; AI Hub protocol 1, pristine client 1.4.0 at 35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869',\n  artDirection:'Original shaded procedural pixel creatures, honeycomb, flowers, greenhouse scenery, hue-shifted materials, native shadows and honey lights',\n  animation:'Native E.Blob spring/squash animation extended with game-owned update/draw rigs for can, worker, express bee, bird, flowers and pageant; native E.anim spray caps',\n  audio:'Original code-synthesized chromatic garden scherzo, effects and Animalese-style gibberish through Web Audio/native engine buses; music defaults to 10%; no audio files',\n  online:'Standalone solo and simultaneous local two-player co-op; AI Hub authoritative shared-world 1–2 player co-op, including server host, snapshots, departures and team finish. No standalone room broker.',\n  testing:'Headless Node simulation and ordinary-input solo/co-op full campaigns; assembled file:// Chromium/WebKit; emulated standard pads and mobile touch; offline audio; official Hub harness including 150ms latency, 50ms jitter, 5% loss, host-leave, server and 1p, plus real two-copy gameplay. Physical hardware, human listening and live catalogue deployment: unknown.',\n  research:'Read Blue Sky Rangers original cartridge manual and developer-alumni history; inspected gameplay reference image; read pinned engine API/FORMATION kit/headless pattern and official Hub protocol/client/example/fixtures. URLs and conclusions in docs/research.md.',\n  environment:'Codex CLI (headless); Linux',model:'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max',usage:'added on import'\n },\n testingFeedback:[\n  \"'`${issues.length} distinct implementation issues were caught and fixed; fixture/assertion mistakes are excluded. Details are in docs/issues.json.`,\n  `${issues.filter(i=>i.critical).length} critical issue: translated custom actors were invisible because the native crop tracker ignored their Canvas transforms.`,\n  '\"'The ordinary-input full campaigns proved the complete six-garden loop; actual two-copy Hub spray/call/departure tests then found problems that protocol conformance alone missed.',\n  'Boot-only checks were least diagnostic: they passed while custom actors were invisible. A focused visual check exposed the missing crop bounds.'\n ],\n engineFeedback:[\n  'Native pixel primitives, palettes, rig springs, lighting, input bindings and controller-navigable Shell supplied a coherent base without external assets.',\n  'Yes. Custom local-coordinate transforms silently escaped the tracked actor crop; phone Fill also clamped the arena scale above its usable fit.',\n  'The rendering-independent tactical simulation and one authoritative co-op ledger, including stable reward identities, last-pulse races and harvest-opened shield phases.',\n  'Preserving one fixed arena while extending native rigs and keeping pointer/touch/controller ownership consistent across the Shell and Hub lifecycle.',\n  'Two small engine patches: transform-aware actor drawing bounds prevent invisible translated/scaled rigs; fractional native Fill preserves the complete arena on small low-density screens. Other additions are game code.',\n  'Add an explicit documented local-coordinate actor drawing contract with transformation-aware crop bounds and a small visual regression example.'\n ],\n promptFeedback:[\n  'The distinctive source mechanics, native art/audio constraints and permission to use headless testing encouraged a complete, original arcade game.',\n  'PLAN.md names a different effort/context budget. TASK.md and the actual assigned model metadata were used for the deliverable names and reporting.',\n  'Finishing the whole tactical campaign, native device UX and authoritative shared-world co-op together in one portable HTML.',\n  'Supply a machine-readable release metadata template and a minimal official Hub test runner alongside the engine handoff.'\n ],\n aiHub:{name:rel.title,tagline:'Spritz responsibly. Feed extravagantly.',description:'Defend a garden party with a very small spray can and a very particular hummingbird. Turn bees into tactical honeycomb, manage your parking space and feed red parcels to crack the pageant shields across six gardens.',type:'Game',genre:'Shooter',source:'Buzz Bombers (1983)',series:'',players:'1–2',controls:'A/D or stick move; Space/Cross/R2 spray; E/Square call Pip; Escape/Options pause; mouse column aim; touch drag and tap combs.',tags:['arcade','co-op','pixel art','retro','comedy','boss fights']}\n};\nwriteFileSync(new URL('../exit-interview.json',root),JSON.stringify(data,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nEOF\nnode tools/write-interview.mjs\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='tools/build.mjs';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"<script>\"'${escaped(read('\"'vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js'))}</script>\\\",\\\"<script>/*\"'! ${read('\"'vendor/engine/LICENSE')} */\\\\\\\\n\"'${escaped(read('\"'vendor/engine/my-3d2dge.js'))}</script>\\\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnode tools/build.mjs --quiet\nnode tools/test.mjs build\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
