{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_103","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n# Buzz Comb Party — complete\n\n## Hand-in\n\n- Playable self-contained release in this workspace root: \"'`Buzz-Comb-Party-Buzz-Bombers-1983-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-045748.html`.\n- Required root interview: `exit-interview.json` (exact TASK.md schema, parsed and validated).\n- All source, vendored inputs, tools, docs, tests and evidence are in `Buzz-Comb-Party-Buzz-Bombers-1983-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-045748/`.\n- Source title selected with Node crypto.randomInt: draw 25 of 50 privately brainstormed riffs.\n\n## Finished scope\n\nSix authored gardens; complete ordinary win/loss/retry/replay; swept two-bee spray; workers and express bees; tactical comb routes and real hive pockets; Pip'\"'s flight/feed/call/irritation/retreat; warned flowers, safe relocation and enclosure recovery; one score/stock ledger with finite retry/rescue rewards; one rehearsal shield and three finale buds; native original procedural pixel rigs, animations, garden lighting/shadows and code-only music/effects/gibberish; native menus, settings, bindings and paged About; controller/mouse/keyboard/touch controls; exclusive simultaneous local co-op devices; exact ten-second attract loop; pause/developer tools, live tuning/reset, import/export and content validation; Hub authoritative 1–2-player co-op and server host.\n\nEngine: my-3D2dge 0.89.1, pinned revision \"'`8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691`. Two marked, documented engine changes: transformed custom-actor crop bounds and native Fill downscaling. Hub protocol 1/client 1.4.0 at `35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869`; released session client remains byte-identical as first head script. Original licenses/notices preserved; engine MIT license included in final HTML.\n\n## Final verification\n\nFrom the development directory:\n\n```sh\nnpm run build\nnpm test\n```\n\nFinal complete suite: **Checks: 155 passed, 0 failed**. All tests cover the final assembled HTML where appropriate. The suite prints only failures and its one final count. `npm test -- sim|browser|hub|build` selects a focused group. No test rerun is needed unless covered code changes.\n\n- Ordinary-input solo: 622.825 seconds, 177,700 score, 4 reserves remaining.\n- Ordinary-input co-op: 617.458 seconds, 212,200 score, 4 shared reserves remaining.\n- Both complete all six encounters and four shield buds with normal stock/ammo/cooldowns, without teleports, actor deletion, forced phase changes or protection.\n- Official Hub harness passes: 2p, 150ms latency / 50ms jitter / 5% loss, host-leave, server host, and 1p. Additional real-copy gameplay verifies conversion/score, remote calls, live local options, malformed input rejection, enclosure/reset, client departure, one finish, and no ticks/sends after end.\n- Chromium/WebKit, emulated controller and actual CDP multi-touch checks pass. Touch steering persists its target; context Harvest and safe auto-fire work. Orientation preserves geometry and centering. Denied storage and copied-away HTML boot pass.\n- Offline audio is finite, non-silent and unclipped; 10% gain ratio and exact mute verified. No human listening review.\n- Visual evidence reviewed: title, busy wave/flower warning, finale, pause/dev tools, results, paged About, phone title and landscape. Ten material issues fixed, two critical; all logged and verified in `docs/issues.json`.\n\nFinal artifact: 1,414,793 bytes; SHA-256 `a01c324267124116449860c381655e6d06b1f28daa1f2c8265c106a763ff0ced`.\n\n## Handoff and limits\n\nREADME, research/provenance, contracts/wire schema, content guide with two examples, engine-change notes and detailed test report are complete. Required Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback are in the game'\"'s paged About and root interview; final response must also contain them. Usage is \"'`added on import`; assigned model is OpenAI, gpt-6.1-s